# =============================================================================
# .gitignore - GHS Chemical Hazard Classification
# =============================================================================
# GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB and is not a data repository.
# This project generates roughly 8 GB of intermediate arrays, so the split is:
#
#   GitHub  ->  code, figures, manuscript, results tables, the deployed model
#   Zenodo  ->  the datasets, the descriptor matrices, the large models
#
# Everything excluded here is REGENERATED by re-running the pipeline, or is
# archived on Zenodo and cited by DOI. Nothing is lost.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Python environment -----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/

# ---- Large numeric arrays (regenerate with Steps 4 and 6) -------------------
# features/STEP4_X.npy alone is 757 MB; the nine balanced training sets are
# 606 MB each.
*.npy
*.npz
features/STEP6_balanced/
colab_results/

# ---- Large datasets (archive on Zenodo, cite the DOI) -----------------------
# Regenerate with Steps 2 and 3, or download from the Zenodo record.
STEP2_raw_ghs_dataset.csv
STEP3_cleaned_ghs_dataset.csv
STEP3_modelling_subset.csv
STEP4_feature_matrix.csv
STEP4_feature_matrix.csv.gz
STEP4_label_matrix.csv
features/STEP4_compound_index.csv
data/raw/
data/cleaned/
data/splits/*.csv

# The compound index (43 MB) and the compressed feature matrix (29 MB) sit
# under GitHub's 100 MB hard limit but above its 50 MB warning threshold, and
# both are pure derived data. Keeping them out takes the repository from 99 MB
# to about 27 MB, which clones quickly. Step 4 regenerates both.

# The cached PubChem annotation pages - about 350 MB, purely a download cache.
data/raw/_annotation_pages/

# ---- Large model files (Zenodo) ---------------------------------------------
# The Random Forests are 90-103 MB each and exceed GitHub's limit. The
# gradient-boosting model that the application actually uses is only 5.5 MB and
# IS tracked - see the exception below.
models/*.pkl
!models/STEP8_xgb_tuned.pkl
models/*.csv

# ---- Run artefacts ----------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
interface/verification_report.pdf
interface/benzene_v4.pdf

# ---- OS / editor ------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ---- Streamlit local state --------------------------------------------------
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ---- Zenodo upload archive --------------------------------------------------
# The data archive built by src/build_zenodo_archive.py is ~366 MB, far over
# GitHub's 100 MB file limit, and is published at its own DOI
# (10.5281/zenodo.21876611). The README and the form guide beside it are small
# and stay tracked, because they document what the archive contains.
zenodo_data_archive/*.zip

# ---- Word lock files ---------------------------------------------------------
# Created the moment a .docx is opened for review and deleted when it closes.
# `git add -A` swept two of these into earlier commits while the manuscript
# was open for the very review that caught the defects those commits fixed.
~$*.doc*
